  scope: HTTP handlers and helpers exclusively serving automation execution history endpoints. Three exported handler methods (ListHistory, ListAutomationHistory, GetHistoryDetail) plus their dedicated query-string parser (parseHistoryFilter). The "// ── History ──" section header comment moves with these handlers; the "// ── Helpers ──" header that immediately followed in the original file remains in automation_handler.go to mark the notifyReload/checkWebhookTokenUniqueness section. Audit-log writes (h.auditor.Log*) live with their respective lifecycle handlers (Create/Update/Delete in automation_handler_crud.go, Toggle/ReEnable in automation_handler.go) and stay there — the "history/audit" sub-area in this prompt is execution-history endpoints, not automation lifecycle audit recording.
  identifiers_moved (3 exported methods + 1 unexported method on *AutomationHandler; preserved in source order):
    automation_handler_history.go (3 exported methods, 1 unexported method):
      - func (h *AutomationHandler) ListHistory(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)
          GET /automations/history. Lists recent execution history across all automations with optional ?status, ?since, ?limit, ?offset filters. Calls pagination, h.parseHistoryFilter (now in same file), h.historyRepo.ListAll, h.historyRepo.GetStats, writeJSON. Wraps the result in historyListResponse (defined in automation_handler_dtos.go).
      - func (h *AutomationHandler) ListAutomationHistory(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)
          GET /automations/{id}/history. Same as ListHistory but scoped to a single automation; first verifies the automation exists via h.getByID (cross-file, in automation_handler.go). Calls urlParamInt64, pagination, h.parseHistoryFilter, h.historyRepo.ListAll, h.historyRepo.GetStats, writeJSON, writeError.
      - func (h *AutomationHandler) GetHistoryDetail(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request)
          GET /automations/history/{historyId}. Returns one execution record plus FSM transitions during the execution window. Calls urlParamInt64, h.historyRepo.GetByID, h.historyRepo.GetStats, h.fsmTransRepo.Query, writeJSON, writeError. Wraps the result in historyDetailResponse (defined in automation_handler_dtos.go).
      - func (h *AutomationHandler) parseHistoryFilter(r *http.Request) database.HistoryFilter
          Method helper used exclusively by ListHistory and ListAutomationHistory (verified via grep: 2 callers, both moving to this file). Parses ?status and ?since query params (RFC3339 then date-only) into a database.HistoryFilter.
